Description: Estimation of the lifetime distribution of
    discrete-time data subject to random left-truncation and right-censoring,
    including competing risks, with applications to loan-level data from
    asset-backed securities (ABS). Provides hazard rate, distribution, and
    cumulative incidence function estimates with asymptotic confidence
    intervals, plotting methods, and tools for computing the actuarial present
    value and risk-adjusted internal rate of return of a loan, following
    Lautier, Pozdnyakov, and Yan (2023) <doi:10.1016/j.ecosta.2023.05.005>
    and Lautier, Pozdnyakov, and Yan (2025) <doi:10.1214/25-AOAS2103>.
